ADC-Based LED Control using LPC2148
ADC reads analog voltage from input pin. Converted digital value is stored in ADC register. 
Program compares ADC value with threshold (512). 
// threshold value simply means set point, or boundary when it reached triggers a specific state
LED glows if value exceeds threshold.
Converts analog signal into digital value.
Turns ON LED when ADC value is greater than 512.
Turns OFF LED when ADC value is less than or equal to 512.
